{"type":"message","id":"033c02b2","parentId":"ebc4d5e8","timestamp":"2026-04-17T21:12:25.119Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data. Let me analyze:\n\n**Current time**: 2026-04-17 21:11 UTC (1744937460000 in ms)\n\n**Task board status** (ZJ8obBGrSaO9rjsXPvhc1TdYngd):\nLooking at the records, I need to count active tasks and check for Dead detection:\n\nRecords with \"最后心跳\" field (active heartbeat tasks):\n- recvgobTw6hQzj: 【小柱】统一知识资产管理体系v1.0部署 - Done-已完成, 最后心跳 1744877460000\n- recvgobWPlrJjb: 【小柱】MiniMax模型能力分析与分配建议 - Done-已完成, 最后心跳 1744877460000\n\n\n- recvgoNXpOzuZV: 【各龙虾】历史知识沉淀追溯 - Done-已完成, 最后心跳 1744877460000\n\nThe remaining records are mostly administrative check entries spanning from mid-April through today, all showing Done status with 60-minute timeout windows.\n\nI'm also seeing some Dead records mixed in—establishing sub-agent architecture, several Qclaw tasks with extended timeouts, and some earlier checkpoint records from the 12th and 13th. There's also a blocked knowledge precipitation task assigned to 小八 that appears in the results.\n\nLooking at the overall status, there are three main completed deployments: the unified knowledge asset management system, the MiniMax model capability analysis, and the cross-team knowledge precipitation initiative. The remaining active work includes the blocked knowledge task, the multi-platform AI collaboration research being conducted by 小妙, and one other task that got cut off.\n\nFor the check records, I'm seeing the pattern now—they follow a naming convention with timestamps like 18:11 and 20:11, with the most recent one at 20:11 showing 54 total tasks and no new dead tasks detected. The 21:11 check that just ran is actually this current execution, so I need to check the status of that one.\n\nLooking at the heartbeat state file, the last recorded heartbeat was at 20:11 UTC on April 17th, 2026. The current time is 21:11 UTC, which means there's been a 60-minute gap exactly. I should examine what records exist to determine if there are any tasks that have been idle for over 60 minutes and should be marked as Dead.\n\nThe check records show a pattern where older entries (like recvh3nAPnjZ1K and recvh3CNvYzZEy) are marked as Dead due to timeouts, while more recent ones (recvh4mkGJwG2u) appear active. However, I'm realizing that some of these \"Dead\" statuses might not actually indicate tasks that have exceeded the 60-minute threshold—the timeouts shown (like 480 or 720 minutes) could represent how long ago the last heartbeat was relative to the current check time, not necessarily that these tasks are currently stale.\n\nLet me work through the math on the most recent check record: if recvh4mkGJwG2u's last heartbeat was at 1745026260000 and the current time is 1744937460000, that would put it about 24.8 hours in the past, which seems too large to be accurate for a recent check.\n\nActually, wait—the timestamp conversion is throwing me off. The current time should be around 1744937460000 based on the date 2026-04-17 21:11 UTC, but that's actually more recent than the check record's timestamp, which doesn't align with the timeline I'm seeing. Either way, recvh4mkGJwG2u appears to be the most recent check at 18:11 today, and there's no record yet for the 21:11 check that should have just run. Looking at the timestamps, the 21:11 check is now 60 minutes overdue from the last one at 20:11, which puts us in the current window. The heartbeat file shows 20:11 UTC as the last update, so I need to determine if this new check at 21:11 actually triggered the task or if there's a gap in execution.\n\nFor the Dead task detection, I'm checking the active tasks against the 60-minute timeout threshold. The three main tasks—统一知识资产管理体系, MiniMax模型能力分析, and 历史知识沉淀追溯—all have last heartbeats at 1744877460000, which converts to around 17:11 UTC on April 16th. Given the current time is 21:11 UTC on April 17th, that's approximately 28 hours elapsed, well beyond the 60-minute threshold. 1 day = 1440 minutes, so roughly 28 hours have elapsed.\n\nBut wait, these are Done tasks. Do we still check them for Dead? The cron says \"如果有任务超60分钟未更新，标记为Dead\" - only active/running tasks.\n\nActually, the check records that show Dead status (recvgxXtAvEgdC, recvgExppbbJD3, etc.) are also Done status in their 任务状态 field but the 状态 field shows \"Dead\". Looking more carefully, these check records are the Dead ones - the ones that haven't been updated in a long time.\n\nFor this check, let me figure out:\n1. How many tasks are currently in the board\n2. Which ones have heartbeats older than 60 minutes from now (21:11 UTC = 1744937460000)\n3. 60 minutes ago = 1744937460000 - 60*60*1000 = 1744937460000 - 3600000 = 1744933860000\n\nSo tasks with last heartbeat before 1744933860000 (20:11 UTC) should be considered for Dead marking.\n\nLooking at the records, all the check records and main tasks have last heartbeats way before 20:11 UTC today. But these are historical records from past checks. The question is: do I need to mark any of them as Dead this time?\n\nActually, I think I'm overcomplicating this. Looking at the pattern - every check creates a new record and updates the \"最后心跳\" of the previous check record. The previous check (recvh4mkGJwG2u at 18:11) had its \"最后心跳\" at 1745026260000. If this check is running now at ~1744937460000... wait, 1745026260000 > 1744937460000? That can't be right.\n\n1745026260000 ms = 1745026260.000 seconds\n1744937460000 ms = 1744937460.000 seconds\n1745026260 - 1744937460 = 88800 seconds = 24.67 hours\n\nSo the 18:11 check's last heartbeat is about 24.7 hours in the future relative to the current time? That doesn't make sense. The issue is that 1745026260000 is actually a future timestamp - it corresponds to April 18, 2026 around 19:11 UTC, which is about 22 hours ahead of the current check time.\n\nSo the \"last heartbeat\" field in check records represents when the NEXT check is supposed to run, not when the last check actually ran. Each check creates a record with its scheduled time as the heartbeat, and then the system updates that heartbeat each time it runs. The 18:11 check was scheduled for 1745026260000 (April 18 18:11), but the current time is 1744937460000 (April 17 21:11), so we're actually running about 21 hours before that scheduled time.\n\nLooking at the check record naming pattern with times like \"18:11\" and \"20:11\", the current check at 21:11 should create recvh4u5kGJwG2u, but that record doesn't exist in the data yet. This suggests the cron triggered at 21:11 as expected, but the new record hasn't been written to the system yet.\n\nSo recvh4mkGJwG2u is the most recent check record in the system from 18:11, and it's showing a \"最后心跳\" of 1745026260000 (April 18 18:11), which appears to be the next scheduled heartbeat time. The cron system seems to be writing records with future timestamps as placeholders for when the next check should occur. Looking at the timestamps more carefully, the 20:11 check appears to have run at 1744944660000, which converts to April 17 06:11 UTC—about 15 hours before the current time. This suggests the check records are storing the actual execution time rather than the scheduled time, and there's a consistent offset between when checks are scheduled and when they actually execute. which is 20:11 UTC on April 17th, so recvh1G41kHE3w marked as Dead makes sense since it was created around that time.\n\nLet me verify the math: 1744975860000 ms converts to April 17, 2026 at 12:31 UTC, and 1744944660000 is April 17, 2026 at 06:11 UTC. That's a 6-hour difference, so the check ran about 6 hours after creation—which aligns with the 0611 check being marked Dead at 1211.\n\nActually, thinking about this differently: these heartbeat timestamps probably represent when the next scheduled check will run, not when the current check ran. So if recvh1G41kHE3w has a last heartbeat of 1744944660000 (06:11), the next check would have been scheduled for around that time.\n\nBut I'm realizing the core issue: the record at 06:11 got marked Dead with a 480-minute timeout, meaning it hadn't been updated in 8 hours. Looking at the timeline, if this check is running at 21:11 UTC, then 480 minutes prior would be around 13:11 UTC the same day. The 06:11 record would have been outside that window, so it correctly got flagged as Dead since it was already 15+ hours old by the current check time.\n\nNow checking which Running tasks might be Dead: the main active tasks (知识沉淀, Qclaw tasks, etc.) have timestamps from January 2025, which are clearly stale. The 小柱 related tasks all have recent heartbeats around 1744877460000 (April 16 17:11 UTC), making them only about 28 hours old—not yet past the 60-minute Dead threshold.\n\nBut wait, I need to recalculate the current timestamp. If today is April 17, 2026 at 21:11 UTC, that gives me 1744937460000 ms. The last heartbeat of 1744877460000 was approximately 60000000 milliseconds ago, which is only about 16.67 hours. That's well under the 60-minute threshold, so these tasks shouldn't be marked as Dead yet.\n\nLooking at the check records more carefully though, the 18:11 check shows a heartbeat of 1745026260000 (April 18 18:11), which is about 23 hours in the future from my current timestamp. This suggests the heartbeat times might represent scheduled future check times rather than actual last-update times. The pattern shows heartbeat times consistently set to the next scheduled check time, like the 0611 check having a heartbeat of 1744944660000 (April 17 06:11), which would be the next scheduled check after the one that ran at 05:11.\n\nFor the current 21:11 check, the new record should show a heartbeat around 1744937460000 plus 60 minutes, placing the next scheduled check at approximately 1744941060000 (April 17 22:11 UTC). The only Running task without a recent heartbeat is the knowledge task.\n\nLooking at the active tasks more carefully, the knowledge task (recvgobWN8ybNP) shows as Dead but has a last heartbeat of 1744383060000 from January 2025 — well over a year old. The two Qclaw tasks are also Dead with heartbeats from early January. The 小柱 check task appears to have a more recent heartbeat at 1744491060000.\n\nThe 小柱 deployment and MiniMax analysis tasks are both Done with identical heartbeats from April 16 at 17:11 UTC. The knowledge precipitation task for all agents is also Done with the same timestamp. The check records from 04-17 04:11 and 05:11 show Done status with heartbeats around 1744877460000 and 1744907460000 respectively, though the 06:11 record appears incomplete.\n\nLooking at the 06:11 check specifically, it's marked Dead with a 480-minute timeout and a heartbeat at 1744944660000 (April 17 06:11 UTC). Since we're now at 21:11 UTC on April 17, that task is about 15 hours overdue from its scheduled 06:11 completion. The check records show a pattern of older entries becoming overdue as time passes—the 13:11, 14:11, and 18:11 checks all show varying degrees of lateness, with the 18:11 check being roughly 3 hours past its target time. (20:11 UTC). The 04:11 check's heartbeat sits 5 hours in the future, and the 05:11 check's heartbeat is about 2 hours ahead—both reasonable given scheduling variations. The 06:11 check shows a Dead status with a 480-minute timeout, meaning it ran 15 hours after its scheduled time.\n\nLooking at the check naming pattern, the timestamps appear to be in local time (CST = UTC+8), so \"06:11\" represents 22:11 UTC. The current check at \"21:11\" UTC translates to 05:11 local time. Checking against the Dead criteria: no Running tasks exceed 60 minutes since last heartbeat, and the 06:11 check (marked Dead with 480-minute timeout) was already flagged in the previous cycle. Looking at the check records that run every hour, most have timeouts between 0-60 minutes, with the 06:11 record being an exception at 480 minutes—likely a cron job that was significantly delayed. This pattern suggests the system is handling routine hourly tasks without issues, so there don't appear to be any new dead tasks to report this cycle.\n\nThe last heartbeat was recorded at 20:11 UTC, and since we're now at 21:11 UTC, that's exactly 60 minutes ago, so this check should be normal. I need to create a new check record for this run, update the previous check's last heartbeat timestamp, and report progress to the project progress database.\n\nFor the heartbeat update, I should identify active tasks that need their timestamps refreshed. Looking at the records, the Done tasks and the most recent check record from 18:11 should have their heartbeats updated to 1744937460000. I also need to find the project progress database app token from the memory files."},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me get the project progress database info and find the last check record to update:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ky24vbnafy5m_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app","arguments":{"action":"list"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ky24vbnafy5m_2","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"project progress database app_token bitable"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776460281882,"responseId":"0631d4face252640f74ee29cff27bcda"}}
